# Polestar Experimental, Riverglades for the Horde, part 2 of 2 (2026-11-11). Hand-written from
# players' recordings (3-14 people per quest), with Forever's quest data for titles, levels and objectives.
# Order: Tran'gul's first errand in Sunnyglade (the Twilight cult's farm town) and back; Na'zok's camp and the ogres
# of Bolder'ok in the hills to the north (levels 40-41); Powderfuse Port and one loop round its coasts (the murlocs
# south-west, the crawlers, Trapclaw and the Eastsea pirates north-east, levels 40-43), Smuggler's Special out to the
# pirates' far camp and the hearth from there to Rog'mar;
# Clubtoe's quests in Sunnyglade; then out through Twilight's Shroud to Kargath (its flight path), where our
# Stranglethorn Vale & Swamp of Sorrows guide (39-43) flies on to Grom'gol.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (players' recordings, 3-14 people each): Tran'gul's quests after
# Show Them How It's Done (part 1); Digging for Answers after Twilight Missives; Smuggler's Paradise after The
# Goblin Trader; Smuggler's Special after Smuggler's Paradise; Clugfist's Decree and Bloodmaster's Ring after Might
# Makes Right; Our Ogre Friend only after the Bloodmaster's Ring bouts.
# Left out on purpose:
# - WANTED: Old Rot-Chum (95120), Twilight No More! (95427): Old Rot-Chum and Chogg'Zac are elites (levels 41-42):
#   each behind a group choice only. Spread the Word (95418) and Land of Giants (95420) after Chogg'Zac send you
#   back across the zone to Rog'mar and Bolder'ok: left out.
# - The Bloodmaster's Ring fights (Pay to Play 94669 and the bouts after it): elite arena fights, for a group. Our
#   Ogre Friend (94733), A Boar's Delight (94734) and A Treat for a Friend (94737) come only after those bouts.
# - Step One: Rock (95183): every recorded player got it from Hamur only after Might Makes Right was handed in,
#   when the rocks lie back east in the hills: left out.
# - Smuggler's Bargain (95294): Captain Haynes sends you back to Friz once more, after the hearth has taken you
#   home. Smuggler's Special is in: you hearth from the pirates' camp right after delivering it.
# - Unworthy Champion (95425): its Skullbasher comes from a fight nobody recorded solo.
# - The Eastsea pirates' second wave (95122, 95123, 95165, 95124): levels 44-45, above this leg.
# - The Wayward Warrior (94744) and Da'grosh's quests: two to three recorded players, levels 41-43.

step Tran'gul
  tip Experimental route (alpha): if a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Tran'gul stands beside Krom'rosh in the middle of Rog'mar: now that the Farholde camp has had its lesson, he has work in Sunnyglade.
  accept 94672                          -- Encroaching Twilight
  accept 94680                          -- Twilight Missives

step Sunnyglade
  tip West of Rog'mar the Twilight cult holds the farm town of Sunnyglade. The Shadowmancers on its northern side carry the missives.
  kill 256952 x8 quest 94672.1          -- Twilight Raider
  kill 254560 x8 quest 94672.2          -- Twilight Shadowmancer
  kill 256798 x8 quest 94672.3          -- Twilight Neophyte
  collect 265745 x3 quest 94680.1 @48.1,47.0  -- Twilight Missive

step Tran'gul
  tip East back to Rog'mar.
  turnin 94672
  turnin 94680
  accept 94727                          -- Digging for Answers: for Clubtoe in Sunnyglade, at the end of this guide

step Na'zok's camp
  tip North-east from Rog'mar up into the hills: Na'zok watches the Paletusk boars from his camp.
  accept 95163                          -- Drive Them Back
  accept 95162                          -- Paletusk Harvesting

step Bolder'ok
  tip North-west to Bolder'ok, the ogres' town. Clugfist, its chieftain, sits on the hill. The ogres are friendly while you leave them alone.
  accept 95424 @64.5,14.9               -- Clugfist: Might Makes Right

step The hills east of Bolder'ok
  tip The Twilight Maulers and Firecallers camp on the ridge east of Na'zok. The Young Paletusks wander the hills south of it: tap them with Na'zok's staff to send them home. The Mature Paletusks around Na'zok's camp drop the boar meat.
  kill 261497 x7 quest 95424.2 @75.7,26.9  -- Twilight Firecaller
  kill 260968 x7 quest 95424.1          -- Twilight Mauler
  use 268521 quest 95163.1 @72.8,39.5   -- Swineherd's Staff, on the Young Paletusks
  collect 769 x10 quest 95162.1 @70.3,31.6  -- Chunk of Boar Meat, from the Mature Paletusks

step Na'zok
  turnin 95163
  turnin 95162

step Bolder'ok
  tip Back to Clugfist on his hill. Jezap Jinglesprocket runs the Bloodmaster's Ring just below it.
  turnin 95424 @64.5,14.9               -- Clugfist
  accept 95428 @64.5,14.9               -- Clugfist's Decree: for Krom'rosh in Rog'mar, at the end of the port loop
  accept 94668 @64.5,14.9               -- Bloodmaster's Ring
  turnin 94668                          -- Jezap Jinglesprocket

step Powderfuse Port
  tip South-east down out of the hills to Powderfuse Port, the goblins' harbour on the coast. Friz Frazzlespark keeps a stall at the west end of the docks, Fimbo Greasemitz cooks by the inn, Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz works the north pier.
  turnin 93976                          -- Friz Frazzlespark: The Goblin Trader
  accept 95288                          -- Smuggler's Paradise
  accept 95121                          -- Fimbo Greasemitz: A Taste of the Sea
  accept 95254 @78.5,53.9               -- The WANTED! poster by the inn: Trapclaw
  accept 95118                          -- Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz: Saltwater Savages
  accept 95119                          -- Unfriendly Competition

step WANTED: Old Rot-Chum
  when group 95120
  tip Old Rot-Chum is an elite (level 42) on the south shore: grouping up is advised.
  accept 95120 @78.5,53.9               -- The WANTED! poster by the inn

step The murlocs, south-west
  tip South-west along the shore from the port: the saltwater murlocs camp on the beaches. The Saltwater Murloc Eyes drop from all of them.
  collect 268344 x12 quest 95121.1 @72.5,67.7  -- Saltwater Murloc Eye
  kill 256801 x8 quest 95118.1          -- Murloc Warrior
  kill 255898 x8 quest 95118.2          -- Murloc Oracle

step Old Rot-Chum
  when onquest 95120
  collect 268341 quest 95120.1 @77.6,72.0  -- Rot-Covered Harpoon

step The crawlers and Trapclaw
  tip Back past the port and north along the beach: the Shore Crawlers drop the meat. Trapclaw, a big crab, scuttles along the rocks east of the docks.
  collect 268345 x6 quest 95121.2 @78.7,49.0  -- Sand Crawler Meat
  collect 268586 quest 95254.1 @83.0,50.5  -- Trapclaw's Pincer

step The Eastsea pirates
  tip North-east along the coast to the pirates' camp on the cliffs. The buccaneers and musketeers carry the smuggled goods.
  kill 257901 x10 quest 95119.1         -- Eastsea Buccaneer
  kill 257910 x10 quest 95119.2         -- Eastsea Musketeer
  collect 268796 x8 quest 95288.1 @86.4,38.1  -- Smuggled Goods

step Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz
  when onquest 95120
  turnin 95120

step Powderfuse Port
  tip Back to the port.
  turnin 95118                          -- Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz
  turnin 95119
  turnin 95254                          -- Fimbo Greasemitz
  turnin 95121
  turnin 95288                          -- Friz Frazzlespark
  accept 95293                          -- Smuggler's Special: for Captain Bentcoin at the pirates' camp

step Captain Bentcoin
  tip Back out along the coast to the far end of the pirates' camp: Captain Bentcoin waits by the water. Then hearth from there.
  turnin 95293 @91.2,39.8

step Hearth to Rog'mar
  hearth "Rog'mar"

step Krom'rosh
  turnin 95428

step Clubtoe
  tip West to Sunnyglade again: Clubtoe, a Twilight miner who wants out, waits at the town's eastern edge. Talk him round, then hand Tran'gul's quest in.
  complete 94727 @49.9,46.9             -- talk Clubtoe round
  turnin 94727
  accept 95417                          -- The Purple Ones
  accept 95602                          -- Sickening Lights
  turnin 95417 @49.3,46.8               -- Twilight Brute, a few steps west
  accept 95601 @49.3,46.8               -- The Purple Ones

step The ritual grounds
  tip The ritualists and their empowered brutes gather at the ritual circles in the middle of Sunnyglade: wreck five of the circles.
  kill 261711 x5 quest 95601.1 @48.0,49.5  -- Empowered Brute
  kill 262169 x10 quest 95601.2 @48.3,49.6  -- Twilight Ritualist
  complete 95602 @47.7,49.8             -- destroy 5 Twilight Ritual Circles

step Clubtoe
  turnin 95601
  turnin 95602

step Chogg'Zac
  when group 95427
  tip Chogg'Zac, the two-headed ogre, is an elite (level 41) at the western edge of Sunnyglade: grouping up is advised.
  accept 95427                          -- Clubtoe: Twilight No More!
  collect 265750 quest 95427.2 @44.8,51.2  -- Chogg's Head
  collect 265751 quest 95427.1 @44.8,51.2  -- Zac's Head
  turnin 95427                          -- Clubtoe

step Twilight's Shroud
  tip The next guide flies from Kargath in the Badlands: walk there and learn its flight path if you don't have it yet. North-west out of Sunnyglade and up the valley to Twilight's Shroud, the way through to the Badlands.
  goto 32.0,29.9 "Twilight's Shroud"

step Kargath
  tip Across the Badlands to Kargath, the Horde fortress built into the cliffs at the zone's western edge: its flight master stands at the foot of the fortress.
  enter "Badlands"
  zone Badlands
  getfp "Kargath"
